{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1261366-backer-version-of-hero-just-dropped","id":1261366,"title":"Backer version of Hero just dropped!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-10-18T13:29:29-07:00","id":1261366,"title":"Backer version of Hero just dropped!","content":"And it is beautiful! I will spend the rest of today rereading it for the art alone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10179-shadryx","name":"shadryx","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-18T13:39:28-07:00","id":1261369,"title":"","content":"Few art pieces are missing, but yeah gotta love the art.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-18T13:45:47-07:00","id":1261373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1261366-backer-version-of-hero-just-dropped?p=1261369#post1261369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Few art pieces are missing, but yeah gotta love the art.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I can't decide if I should note that in the errata thread or not<br /> <br /> Edit: it wasn\u2019t coming through on my reader, but there are apparently notes that say \u201cart in process\u201d, so no it\u2019s not needed as errata.<br /> <br /> But apparently the ancient Tuatha art doesn\u2019t show any of the care toward cultural accuracy that the other pantheons do, so that\u2019s very disappointing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 10-18-2018, 05:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-18T15:22:22-07:00","id":1261401,"title":"","content":"OK: so Sorcerers were removed from <b>Origin</b> (except as Antagonists) because they're too reliant on the Purviews to be doable without access to <b>Hero</b>. Fair enough. But they've been left out of <b>Hero</b>, too. Oversight, or deliberate? If the former, is it too late to correct it? If the latter (or if the former and it's too late to correct), when can we expect to see them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 10-18-2018, 06:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-18T15:42:50-07:00","id":1261407,"title":"","content":"I'm only on the Aesir pantheon, and I'm really confused by the art piece representing them as gods. There's some Aesir that are immediately identifiable: Thor, Odin (though he looks like pirate Gandalf at first glance), Tyr, Loki (amused by the Marvel-esque horned helmet), Hel, etc. But some that are just not..especially the women. None of them seem to match the descriptions by book or myth. If that's supposed to be Frigg next to Odin's throne, that slinky blue Elsa dress is far from &quot;matronly.&quot; Same with who I presume Freya hanging out down by Tyr, who is also described in the book as matronly, but is wearing a tight sleeveless low-cut dress; at least she has the ginger hair from her description. I think that's supposed to Sif holding the rabbit, but where is her golden hair? You know, the <i>very thing</i> she is most famous for in Norse mythology? Or she the one standing by Odin's throne because that lady is blonde and Frigg is the one holding the rabbit. Is it a even a rabbit? Actually, I can't quite tell what animal it is... it just kind of blends in with her dress. See, now I'm just confused... not that it's hard to do with me.<br /> <br /> The artist clearly spent a lot of time and effort on the Aesir, and it's quite lovely as a stand alone piece, but since it's a book illustration and is describing specific characters, it doesn't quite fulfill the job it needs to. I don't think the artist paid attention to the descriptions, assuming they got descriptions at all. I wasn't the biggest fan of the old Pantheon drawings from first edition, but at least I could figure out which god was which from the descriptions in the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23872,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23872-doryna","user":"Doryna","date":". 10-18-2018, 06:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23872-doryna","name":"Doryna","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23872_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-18T15:43:07-07:00","id":1261408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rand Brittain</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The art is better than <i>Origin</i> for the first chapter, but unfortunately, this book has some absolutely dire art. Most of the pantheon pieces are just terrible, and there are plenty that are so horrible I can't believe they're even there, like the one on page 286. I'd put the art as 33% good, 33% great, and 33% absolutely wretched.<br /> <br /> Hopefully some of this stuff gets replaced before the actual final version comes out. Right now it's even worse than Exalted 3e was at first press.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure Ex3 was worse, though for more reasons then just design","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-18T15:54:47-07:00","id":1261414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rand Brittain</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hopefully some of this stuff gets replaced before the actual final version comes out. Right now it's even worse than Exalted 3e was at first press.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ehh... there's a fair amount of bad art here, but I don't think it's Exalted bad. It's really hard to outbad the original 40 cakes. Also, hopefully nothing has been plagiarized, and there are still some &quot;heavily inspired&quot; pieces in the final sale version of Exalted. And while there's a fair share of bad art, none of it that I've seen so far looks like it was made in 15 minutes with a 3d model posing program, and some of that made it into the final Exalted version too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Doryna</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1261366-backer-version-of-hero-just-dropped?p=1261407#post1261407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If that's supposed to be Frigg next to Odin's throne, that slinky blue Elsa dress is far from &quot;matronly.&quot; Same with who I presume Freya hanging out down by Tyr, who is also described in the book as matronly, but is wearing a tight sleeveless low-cut dress; at least she has the ginger hair from her description. I think that's supposed to Sif holding the rabbit, but where is her golden hair? You know, the <i>very thing</i> she is most famous for in Norse mythology? Or she the one standing by Odin's throne because that lady is blonde and Frigg is the one holding the rabbit. Is it a even a rabbit? Actually, I can't quite tell what animal it is... it just kind of blends in with her dress.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm guessing that Freya is the woman holding the animals, which to me looks like cats? Freya's cart/chariot is sometimes described as being pulled by cats, so that's my assumption at least. That said, she's dressed the most conservatively, and she's traditionally the Norse's lust goddess so... that does seem off. Could be Frigg? But I'm not really aware of a cat connection. The blonde's got to be Sif. Pretty much the only mention she gets in the whole mythology is the color of her hair.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest","user":"HighPriest","date":". 10-18-2018, 07:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest","name":"HighPriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2433_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-18T16:52:11-07:00","id":1261431,"title":"","content":"How did you guys like Eric Donner's story?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-18T18:12:34-07:00","id":1261449,"title":"","content":"Dropped for backers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-18T18:17:39-07:00","id":1261451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>omenseer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1261366-backer-version-of-hero-just-dropped?p=1261449#post1261449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dropped for backers?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes the formatted text with most of the art is linked on backerkit. Crowd sourcing errata for it as we speak,","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-18T19:27:21-07:00","id":1261463,"title":"","content":"The pantheon signature preview for the Theoi Metamorphosis the second boon transfigure has the duration listed as Instant. However it talks in the boon about it lasting for Legend 1+ characters a time and trivial characters it being permanent.<br /> <br /> So it says Instant but then last chapter starts with \u201cat the end of this boon.\u201d So when is that it it\u2019s instant? Also, I guess it\u2019s a SG call but do you think they can do anthro forms or other oddities like happen in myths all the time?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6424-fuzzykuma","name":"Fuzzykuma","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-18T20:09:24-07:00","id":1261469,"title":"","content":"That\u2019s probably errata. Put it in the errata thread so we can see whether that is intentional or not","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-18T21:44:34-07:00","id":1261480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1261366-backer-version-of-hero-just-dropped?p=1261431#post1261431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How did you guys like Eric Donner's story?</div> </div> </div> </div>Haven't gotten a chance to read it yet, but I am damned excited to see he's going through a Forge path (at least by the character sheet). Donner was the first time in my near 30 years of rpging that I used a pregenerated character. I played him from Scion to God, and I went the Forge route (well as best I could with Knacks etc). I'm stoked to see that the second go around is following that. Fits with his personality and history.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Things need not have happened to be true. Tales and dreams are the shadow truths that will endure when mere facts are dust and ashes, and forgot.&quot; Sandman (Neil Gaiman)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/733-troller","name":"Troller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar733_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-19T01:16:57-07:00","id":1261510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rand Brittain</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The art is better than <i>Origin</i> for the first chapter, but unfortunately, this book has some absolutely dire art. Most of the pantheon pieces are just terrible, and there are plenty that are so horrible I can't believe they're even there, like the one on page 286. I'd put the art as 33% good, 33% great, and 33% absolutely wretched.<br /> <br /> Hopefully some of this stuff gets replaced before the actual final version comes out. Right now it's even worse than Exalted 3e was at first press.</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot of this art is brutally bad (or like, clearly unfinished), but most of these Pantheon spreads are horrid. What's with all the like, photoshop-y looking faces and weird airbushing? The Netjer have an okay-ish one, though Bast's cat face is awful, and why they went for &quot;puffy human face&quot; and a &quot;drying my armpits&quot; pose over &quot;cow head&quot; for Het-Heru is a mystery to me.<br /> <br /> Also, because I'm only really qualified to blab about the Netjer: <br /> <br /> Section looks good, and a lot better than the draft I raised a stink about ages ago. I'm not quite sure why the Bast writeup seems to suggest she has two names and only presents one, or why it lists Sekhmet as an alias of hers only to devote an entire sidebar to them being different deities.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure why they went for the mob boss of the dead who helps people return to life in exchange for favors angle on Wesir. Like I said in the past, the Netjer are a pantheon where death is final, where even Wesir himself could not return to proper life among the living! Such a weird angle, and one that clearly just feels like Hades with an Egyptian hat.<br /> <br /> Very glad we got Ma'at as allied Titan, that the cosmology all got cleaned up, and that the Path Skills ditched Deception.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-19T01:25:57-07:00","id":1261511,"title":"","content":"Also, am I blind, or are there no mechanics for the various types (Born, Chosen, etc) of Scion?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-19T04:29:02-07:00","id":1261521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1261366-backer-version-of-hero-just-dropped?p=1261511#post1261511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, am I blind, or are there no mechanics for the various types (Born, Chosen, etc) of Scion?</div> </div> </div> </div>There isn't. Because for the most part they all function pretty much the same, any differences is brought through by Paths and even then you dont have it streamed line. The only that really is supposed to be different though is Incarnate, I remember Neall once saying he wished to detail rules about them in God but I'm not sure if that still holds up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-19T05:01:11-07:00","id":1261529,"title":"","content":"I think &quot;different mechanics for the different types of Scion's&quot; is one of those things that, you know, WAS going to be a thing but which they thankfully thought better of and dropped.<br /> <br /> It's just a flavor thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/728-crownedsun","name":"CrownedSun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar728_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"217"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-19T06:17:38-07:00","id":1261544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1261366-backer-version-of-hero-just-dropped?p=1261511#post1261511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, am I blind, or are there no mechanics for the various types (Born, Chosen, etc) of Scion?</div> </div> </div> </div>There aren\u2019t any at this point. The Incarnate are going to have a special relationship with Fate as they scale up, because the narrative of the divinity they\u2019re inheriting is so strong; but other than that they all work the same way and only vary as individuals as far as we know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-19T06:19:57-07:00","id":1261545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1261366-backer-version-of-hero-just-dropped?p=1261521#post1261521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There isn't. Because for the most part they all function pretty much the same, any differences is brought through by Paths and even then you dont have it streamed line. The only that really is supposed to be different though is Incarnate, I remember Neall once saying he wished to detail rules about them in God but I'm not sure if that still holds up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Last I remember hearing, we\u2019re getting a bit of an expansion on them in the Companion because that is exclusively how Nemetondevos Scions exist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-19T08:13:19-07:00","id":1261567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HighPriest</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1261366-backer-version-of-hero-just-dropped?p=1261414#post1261414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm guessing that Freya is the woman holding the animals, which to me looks like cats? Freya's cart/chariot is sometimes described as being pulled by cats, so that's my assumption at least. That said, she's dressed the most conservatively, and she's traditionally the Norse's lust goddess so... that does seem off. Could be Frigg? But I'm not really aware of a cat connection. The blonde's got to be Sif. Pretty much the only mention she gets in the whole mythology is the color of her hair.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, cats! I'll bet you're right, it is a cat and therefore makes it Freya. That makes her fit more with the description. Doesn't explain why Sif is hanging by Odin dressed like Elsa, And why Frigg is lookin' all &quot;matronly&quot; by Tyr, but that still clears some things up. And as clever as the modern boardroom version is, it doesn't help me figure out who is who in the classic version.<br /> <br /> Having looked at all the Pantheons, some of the pictures for them are definitely better than others. I think I like the Theoi and Shen the best; the former is hilarious because there's clearly a story going on there (I love Artemis and Athena's &quot;over it&quot; looks as Ares and Poseidon fight), and the Shen art is just lovely and stylistically appropriate; I'm wondering how the &quot;modern&quot; one is going to look. The others I'm more &quot;that pretty good&quot; or at least &quot;meh&quot; on, but I can at least figure out who most everyone is supposed to be between the classic and modern versions. Also, is it just me, or is someone missing from the Netjer picture?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23872-doryna","name":"Doryna","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23872_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-19T17:18:08-07:00","id":1261671,"title":"","content":"I have to be missing something, but in the Callings and Knacks section of Character Creation it says that a hero has two dots in one calling and one in each of the other two, but all of the pregen characters have five and in the traits section there are a few mentions of a Legend 1 Hero having 5 dots. Seems like there should be a mention of one more dot to throw in somewhere, but I don't see where it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3776-autodefenestrate","name":"AutoDefenestrate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3776_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-19T17:43:22-07:00","id":1261677,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:red\">Hey folks, if you\u2019re going to comment on the artwork, please be sure to keep it respectful. Avoid value judgments like \u201chorrible\u201d and stick to expressions of personal preference like \u201cnot my style.\u201d</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-19T20:34:42-07:00","id":1261699,"title":"","content":"I really wish the example Relics would clearly break down the point value of each individual trait of the relic, instead of just giving the total cost. Even Scion: Hero 1e listed the point values of a relic's unique power(s).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-19T21:17:24-07:00","id":1261710,"title":"","content":"Guys,can anyone help me identify who is Baldr in the Aesir art?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-19T21:42:25-07:00","id":1261714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1261366-backer-version-of-hero-just-dropped?p=1261710#post1261710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Guys,can anyone help me identify who is Baldr in the Aesir art?</div> </div> </div> </div>Follow the line of sight from the mistletoe's scope :3<br /> I think in the mythic picture its the one on the far left with the plant, in the mordern one I think its either the one on the left holding his glasses or the one just past the guy reaching for the wolf figure. At least to my figuring since those two seem to be dressed the least upscale to me of that group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-19T21:49:49-07:00","id":1261718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1261366-backer-version-of-hero-just-dropped?p=1261714#post1261714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Follow the line of sight from the mistletoe's scope :3<br /> I think in the mythic picture its the one on the far left with the plant, in the mordern one I think its either the one on the left holding his glasses or the one just past the guy reaching for the wolf figure. At least to my figuring since those two seem to be dressed the least upscale to me of that group.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought the one with the plant was freyr?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-19T22:29:13-07:00","id":1261727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1261366-backer-version-of-hero-just-dropped?p=1261718#post1261718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought the one with the plant was freyr?</div> </div> </div> </div>Possible, I'm not sure. I mean Baldr's appearance isn't actually that notable among gods, I mean exceptionally attractive is pretty standard affair for most divinities. At which point you're looking for signs, but Baldr was known for prophetic visions of his own death, being the subject of a game where everyone threw lethal stuff at him since all of it had promised not hurt him, and then dying when Loki went and ruined the joke by finding the thing that wasn't in on the deal. None of those are exactly as noticable as Odin missing an eye, Hela being half-corpse, Thor having Mjolnir, or that Ganesh seems to be the nice one who brought snacks in both pictures.To that end it could also be the far right since Hella is staring at him (and amusingly the rigging on the ship does look like an arrow).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-19T22:50:12-07:00","id":1261729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1261366-backer-version-of-hero-just-dropped?p=1261727#post1261727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Possible, I'm not sure. I mean Baldr's appearance isn't actually that notable among gods, I mean exceptionally attractive is pretty standard affair for most divinities. At which point you're looking for signs, but Baldr was known for prophetic visions of his own death, being the subject of a game where everyone threw lethal stuff at him since all of it had promised not hurt him, and then dying when Loki went and ruined the joke by finding the thing that wasn't in on the deal. None of those are exactly as noticable as Odin missing an eye, Hela being half-corpse, Thor having Mjolnir, or that Ganesh seems to be the nice one who brought snacks in both pictures.To that end it could also be the far right since Hella is staring at him (and amusingly the rigging on the ship does look like an arrow).</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooh neat,thank you","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-20T00:37:45-07:00","id":1261739,"title":"","content":"Hmm, so Frigg still makes her Scions vow not to harm Baldr. You think that just means they're not allowed to physically harm him or are they not allowed to kill his Scions because that would cause emotional harm? I've seen it go both ways in stories, so I'm unsure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-20T09:56:12-07:00","id":1261783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AutoDefenestrate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1261366-backer-version-of-hero-just-dropped?p=1261671#post1261671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to be missing something, but in the Callings and Knacks section of Character Creation it says that a hero has two dots in one calling and one in each of the other two, but all of the pregen characters have five and in the traits section there are a few mentions of a Legend 1 Hero having 5 dots. Seems like there should be a mention of one more dot to throw in somewhere, but I don't see where it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay so when writing, Neall got his mental wires crossed and for part of it was writing up how to convert an Origin character (who has one dot in one Calling) into a Hero. So your character should have 5 Calling Dots, with at least 1 dot in each Calling.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1etYiuHfHR-nTI5obsKhL44stbRmLkuvw2Z6qae_lbWM\" target=\"_blank\">I'll just shamelessly plug an FAQ I've been putting together from the Discord talks</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-21T05:35:15-07:00","id":1261924,"title":"","content":"This is probably me just being sensitive due to the fact that I am a modern day Kemetic who is a followet of Bast, but making Bast an alcoholic really confused and upset me. I don't understand why Bast was chosen to be the goddess of prophecy, when Bast is mainly a protector goddess as She is an Eye of Ra. <br /> That being said, it made me very happy to see Bastet as a different goddess in her own right due to many reasons, mostly the Romanization and strange modern beliefs of the dance/perfume/sex connection.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2197-roleplayrose","name":"roleplayrose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2197_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-21T19:56:20-07:00","id":1262039,"title":"","content":"I think the alcohol connection comes from the tale where the lion goddess (variously given as Bast or Sekhmet) wiped out most of humanity at the behest of Re, until she was tricked into drinking enough wine to render her unconscious, thus saving us from extermination. The association of Bast with celebration and revelry also ties in with drink. Prophecy might simply be a way to make her a bit more cosmopolitan for purposes of the game it would also make you a better guardian if you know what's coming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-22T13:26:10-07:00","id":1262210,"title":"","content":"So I might be missing something, but in the Hero preview there are a bunch of black circles in boxes around the character creation section. Is that how its supposed to look? Its like: Box Black Circle next to the words Character Creation example, then actual example. <br /> My first instinct was to put it in errata, but I don't know if I'm missing something on this and figured I'd ask.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-22T15:14:13-07:00","id":1262233,"title":"","content":"Those black spaces are places art will be but isn\u2019t ready","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-22T15:35:40-07:00","id":1262240,"title":"","content":"Okay not sure if this is Errata needed or not but I wanted to ask here. If people think this should be Errata please say and I will repost. <br /> <br /> Okay, so regarding upgrading a Origin character to Hero, it looks like the option in origin to take 2 additional knacks is RAW far worse than taking 4 points of birthrights if you know your game will move to Hero.<br /> As hero states on page 171 your Knacks cap at owning 5, so if I have brought the extra 2 I only gain 2 more. But this isn't the same for Birthrights at 7, it doesn't say that is a cap.<br /> Does this mean I can buy 4 dots of birthrights at the Origin level, then get an extra 7 when I hit hero for a total of 11? This also seems like a problem for a protracted Origin game, buying knacks is at a serious disadvantage if the XP you spend on them is ignored when hitting Hero as you level up to 5 knacks anyway, but your allies who brought Birthrights just get more and can match you on knacks. <br /> <br /> Am I misreading this? <br /> It feels like it should be gain 4 new Knacks and 7 birthrights - but without the limit that is put on knacks, instead just the limit of 5 active knacks at once.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Find my Homebrew so far here: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/18X_mkFwDcM0sSN9R2GoQ72Q5FqW1deFgEM3HIGneABQ/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> So far its Demon Merits, Vampire 1e to 2e ports and a Knowledge collection mechanic for the Ordo Dracul!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24597-lordofiron","name":"LordofIron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24597_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-22T18:24:27-07:00","id":1262264,"title":"","content":"I haven't received any e-mails on this, and I can't seem to access my backerkit account. Does anyone have any advice?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-22T18:28:23-07:00","id":1262266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1261366-backer-version-of-hero-just-dropped?p=1262039#post1262039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the alcohol connection comes from the tale where the lion goddess (variously given as Bast or Sekhmet) wiped out most of humanity at the behest of Re, until she was tricked into drinking enough wine to render her unconscious, thus saving us from extermination. The association of Bast with celebration and revelry also ties in with drink. Prophecy might simply be a way to make her a bit more cosmopolitan for purposes of the game it would also make you a better guardian if you know what's coming.</div> </div> </div> </div>The prophecy thing at least isn't upsetting. Weird but not upsetting. However, it was definitely Sekhmet who drank beer dyed red. Sekhmet was originally a form of Het-Hert that came out when She was asked to punish the humans by Ra. Bast had nothing to do with it. But again... I respect that this is a sensitive subject for me. She is my Mom. She means a lot to me. Worshipping Her saved my life. I just gotta compartmentalize.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2197-roleplayrose","name":"roleplayrose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2197_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-22T22:31:02-07:00","id":1262291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shkspr1048</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1261366-backer-version-of-hero-just-dropped?p=1262264#post1262264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't received any e-mails on this, and I can't seem to access my backerkit account. Does anyone have any advice?</div> </div> </div> </div>Go here: <a href=\"https://scion-2nd-edition-tabletop-rpg.backerkit.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://scion-2nd-edition-tabletop-rpg.backerkit.com/</a> Put in the same email you used for the Kickstarter, and you should get an email with your special unique code.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-22T23:22:13-07:00","id":1262299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>roleplayrose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1261366-backer-version-of-hero-just-dropped?p=1262266#post1262266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The prophecy thing at least isn't upsetting. Weird but not upsetting. However, it was definitely Sekhmet who drank beer dyed red. Sekhmet was originally a form of Het-Hert that came out when She was asked to punish the humans by Ra. Bast had nothing to do with it. But again... I respect that this is a sensitive subject for me. She is my Mom. She means a lot to me. Worshipping Her saved my life. I just gotta compartmentalize.</div> </div> </div> </div>My understanding is that that is one version of the story, and that there are dozens if not hundreds more, some versions which do put a link between Bast and Sekhmet.<br /> <br /> The Kemetic stories have many different variations that have cropped up over the literal millennia of the Egyptian history and culture. Neall has mentioned many a time in the Discord that trying to stick to an ideal singular Mythic Truth is especially difficult, or damn near impossible to achieve, as these stories have shifted and evolved in countless ways throughout history.<br /> <br /> I mean, the first version I heard of the Sehkmet story is that she was born from Re directly when he removed his eye, and Bast or Het-Heru (depending on your version) was born from Sehkmet after she got drunk. Whose version is right? The answer is probably &quot;If you had a time machine and could go back to the right era and ask... You'd probably get a dozen answers depending on what region you hear the story in&quot;<br /> <br /> To be clear, I feel for you and am sorry that this hurt you. But the problem is that there's really no One True Myth that was written down and has endured since, for anything. Stories change with their cultures.<br /> <br /> That said Neall doesn't have the budget to allocate Canon Enforcement Ninjas. If you want to shift Bast's Purviews around a bit then by all means, go ahead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 10-23-2018, 02:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-22T23:37:15-07:00","id":1262302,"title":"","content":"Has there ever been a religion that doesn't have factions, contradictory stories, and entirely disparate teachings? Take what you want from your faith - what it gives you is what's important.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-23T01:14:04-07:00","id":1262314,"title":"","content":"Overall just not happy with the Netjer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-23T02:48:46-07:00","id":1262319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordofIron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1261366-backer-version-of-hero-just-dropped?p=1262240#post1262240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It feels like it should be gain 4 new Knacks and 7 birthrights - but without the limit that is put on knacks, instead just the limit of 5 active knacks at once.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I suspect the &quot;bring your total knacks known to 5&quot; thing in that chart is probably an outdated part of character creation that snuck in from a previous version, as I agree that it's a bad deal for people who went with or chose to learn more knacks with Origin XP. You should check to see if there's an errata in the errata thread already, or post one if there isn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest","name":"HighPriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2433_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-23T06:37:56-07:00","id":1262350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1261366-backer-version-of-hero-just-dropped?p=1262299#post1262299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My understanding is that that is one version of the story, and that there are dozens if not hundreds more, some versions which do put a link between Bast and Sekhmet.<br /> <br /> The Kemetic stories have many different variations that have cropped up over the literal millennia of the Egyptian history and culture. Neall has mentioned many a time in the Discord that trying to stick to an ideal singular Mythic Truth is especially difficult, or damn near impossible to achieve, as these stories have shifted and evolved in countless ways throughout history.<br /> <br /> I mean, the first version I heard of the Sehkmet story is that she was born from Re directly when he removed his eye, and Bast or Het-Heru (depending on your version) was born from Sehkmet after she got drunk. Whose version is right? The answer is probably &quot;If you had a time machine and could go back to the right era and ask... You'd probably get a dozen answers depending on what region you hear the story in&quot;<br /> <br /> To be clear, I feel for you and am sorry that this hurt you. But the problem is that there's really no One True Myth that was written down and has endured since, for anything. Stories change with their cultures.<br /> <br /> That said Neall doesn't have the budget to allocate Canon Enforcement Ninjas. If you want to shift Bast's Purviews around a bit then by all means, go ahead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes... Kemetic stories often contradict and all are true. I realize I am just being sensitive. I just struggle due to the fact that for me Bast is Bast and Sekhmet is Sekhmet and they don't have a lot in common. Buuuuut... I concede that they are both ancient divine beings and after a few thousand years the stories become muddied. And again... All the stories are true, even when they contradict. I am not saying Neall or anyone else did a bad job. I haven't read the whole book yet but I am digging the vibe quite a lot. <br /> <br /> Kemetic myth is complex, particularly when you consider that the state religion and the personal religion were vastly different. So... Yeah. But I just had to pout a bit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1261366-backer-version-of-hero-just-dropped?p=1262314#post1262314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Overall just not happy with the Netjer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Atamajakki what didn't you like?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2197,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2197-roleplayrose","user":"roleplayrose","date":". 10-23-2018, 09:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2197-roleplayrose","name":"roleplayrose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2197_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-27T01:28:20-07:00","id":1263035,"title":"","content":"Will the final version have more bookmarks related to Purviews and Boons? Having only two, one for general Purviews and one for Pantheon Purviews, seems like too little considering how many there are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/458-indivisible","name":"Indivisible","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-09T00:40:13-08:00","id":1265711,"title":"","content":"I'm glad I'm not the only one who was confused by the Aesir art. I think the author went overboard with redheads. The text is solid though, I feel a better sense of who many of the gods are than I did in 1st edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}